    "description": "The first dinosaur ever given a scientific name, in 1824, from Middle Jurassic rocks of England about 166 million years old. It was a heavy predator 6-7 metres long, with a long, low skull full of blade-like serrated teeth and short but very powerful arms ending in three big hooked claws. It hunted plant-eating dinosaurs along the coasts and river plains of a warm island landscape."
