    "description": "A slender, long-necked theropod about 1.7 metres long from the Late Jurassic of north-western China, about 160 million years ago. Its young had teeth, but the adults lost them all and had a horny beak instead, and they swallowed stones to grind plants in the gut: a meat-eater's descendant turned plant-eater. Its arms were tiny, with stubby fingers. Its name, 'mud lizard that could not escape', comes from skeletons found trapped in ancient mud pits."
