    "description": "The commonest giant plant-eater of the Late Jurassic of western North America, about 155-150 million years ago, up to 18 metres long. Compared with Diplodocus it was shorter and deeper, with a thicker neck held up at a slant, a fairly short tail and a short, boxy head with large nostrils. Its strong, spoon-shaped teeth could crop tough vegetation that other sauropods left alone. Herds of all ages seem to have travelled together."
