    "description": "An early long-necked plant-eater 4-6 metres long from the Early Jurassic of southern Africa, about 200-185 million years ago, a distant cousin of the giant sauropods. It walked on its hind legs and had a small head, leaf-shaped teeth and grasping hands with a huge, curved thumb claw. Its nesting grounds, with clutches of eggs holding curled-up embryos, are among the oldest known: the hatchlings walked on all fours and probably stayed near the nest."
  },
