    "description": "A small heterodontosaurid dinosaur about 70 cm long from the Late Jurassic of north-eastern China, about 158 million years ago. It is famous for a crest of long, stiff bristles, up to 6 cm long, running along its back and tail. Because it belongs to the plant-eating branch of dinosaurs, far from the feathered meat-eaters, it suggests that fuzzy body coverings may have been widespread among dinosaurs. Like its relatives it had a beak and small fangs."
