    "description": "A rat-sized early mammal about 17 cm long from the Late Jurassic of north-eastern China, about 160 million years ago. It belonged to the multituberculates, the 'rodents of the Mesozoic', named for the many cusps on their grinding teeth, and ate seeds, plants, insects and worms. Its very flexible ankles could swivel, letting it scamper over the ground, dig and climb. Multituberculates went on to thrive for over 100 million years."
